  [38;5;153mbindForm[39m also sets [38;5;153maria-invalid[39m and [38;5;153maria-describedby[39m on the failing input so screen readers announce the message —
  cheap here, and painful to retrofit across several forms later.

  [1mTwo behavior changes you're buying:[0m validation failures now appear [3min the page[0m instead of only in the console (that's
  the point, but it is a visible change), and [38;5;153mtype="module"[39m means opening [38;5;153mindex.html[39m from [38;5;153mfile://[39m stops working — you'll
  need [38;5;153mpython3 -m http.server[39m or equivalent. You accepted the second when you chose ES modules; I'm restating it
  because it's the one that bites during a quick manual check.

  Does the shape look right so far? And since the repo has no tooling configured at all, the cheapest moment to add any
  is now, before the module exists:

